 ],
 "literal": "Except for what fate has ordained and settled, on his part / to measure and know his nobility, who indeed are we? / Even when the foster-mother spoke, she did not calm down; in addition to that, / in the dark mountain pool of cool water, many buds blossomed / looking at the blue water-lily with thick petals, an inward smile / having become one with tear-filled eyes, / indeed, the resolve of this beautifully jeweled girl is not in vain!",
 "translation": "Except to accept what fate has ordained, who are we to measure and judge his worth? Even when the foster-mother spoke of the veṟi ritual, she did not calm down. Moreover, looking at the thick-petalled blue water-lily that has blossomed from its tight buds in the dark mountain pool of cool water, she smiled to herself, her eyes filling with tears. Indeed, the resolve of this beautifully jeweled girl is not in vain!",
 "modern": "விதி வகுத்து அமைத்ததைத் தவிர, அவருடைய குணத்தின் பெருமையை அளந்து அறிவதற்கு நாம் யார்? வெறியாட்டு எடுப்பதாகச் செவிலித்தாய் சொல்லியும் அவள் அமைதியடையவில்லை. அதுமட்டுமல்லாமல், குளிர்ந்த நீரையுடைய கரிய சுனையில் பல இதழ்களும் அவிழ்ந்து மலர்ந்த தடித்த இதழ்களையுடைய நீல மலரைப் பார்த்து, தனக்குள்ளே சிரித்து, கண்ணீர் நிறைந்த கண்களை உடையவள் ஆனாள். அழகிய அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த இவளுடைய துணிவு வீணானது அல்ல.",
 "explanation": "The foster-mother is worried about the heroine's declining health and suspects a spirit possession, suggesting a veṟi ritual to appease Murukaṉ. The friend (tōḻi) speaks to herself or to the foster-mother, defending the heroine's deep love and resolve. She points out that the heroine did not agree to the ritual, but instead, upon seeing the blue water-lily in the mountain pool—which reminds her of her lover's eyes or their trysting place—she smiled inwardly with tear-filled eyes. This reaction reveals that her affliction is not due to spirits but due to her deep love for the lord of the hills. The friend asserts that the heroine's silent, firm resolve to remain true to her lover is noble and will not go in vain, as they must trust fate and her lover's return. Key words include veṟiyāḷ (foster-mother/ritual performer), nīlam (blue water-lily), and tuṇivu (resolve).",
 "model": "gemini-3.5-flash",
 "generated": "2026-11-26"
}